{"questions":[{"question_id":"1l1nc41vn","paperTitle":"JEE Advanced 2013 Paper 2 Offline","year":2013,"examDate":2013,"subject":"chemistry","chapter":"p-block-elements","chapterGroup":"inorganic-chemistry","topic":"group-16-elements-oxygen-family","type":"mcqm","marks":4,"negMarks":2,"permalink":"pthe-correct-statements-about-osub3sub-isarep-jee-advanced-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-uftvnlw0x0qydryv","content":"<p>The correct statement(s) about O<sub>3</sub> is(are)</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"O-O bond lengths are equal."},{"identifier":"B","content":"Thermal decomposition of O<sub>3</sub> is endothermic."},{"identifier":"C","content":"O<sub>3</sub> is diamagnetic in nature."},{"identifier":"D","content":"O<sub>3</sub> has a bent structure."}],"correct_options":["A","C","D"],"explanation":"<p>As all electrons are paired, ozone is diamagnetic in nature. The structure is bent or V-shaped. The structure of ozone is resonance hybrid of the two structures with a delocalised p-orbital which covers all three atoms. Because of this, the two O-O bond lengths are equal.</p>\n<p> <img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l1qnnakd/19670a26-b57c-4ad1-bd24-61924de27b35/aff6f5e0-b75a-11ec-8d7d-cfbb317f859a/file-1l1qnnake.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l1qnnakd/19670a26-b57c-4ad1-bd24-61924de27b35/aff6f5e0-b75a-11ec-8d7d-cfbb317f859a/file-1l1qnnake.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2013 Paper 2 Offline Chemistry - p-Block Elements Question 44 English Explanation\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l1qnnakd/19670a26-b57c-4ad1-bd24-61924de27b35/aff6f5e0-b75a-11ec-8d7d-cfbb317f859a/file-1l1qnnake.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l1qnnakd/19670a26-b57c-4ad1-bd24-61924de27b35/aff6f5e0-b75a-11ec-8d7d-cfbb317f859a/file-1l1qnnake.png?format